{"id": "r01", "expected": "BLOCK", "finding": "Grant/policy constraints on 'amount' are one-sided (max only, no min anywhere in the chain or policy); a negative amount (-500) satisfies every max<= check and every approval_over/over_cap check (which only compare '> threshold'), so a refund for -500 ACTs even though no real-world refund grant means 'or take money the other way'.", "severity": "high", "grants": [{"id": "g1", "parent": null, "issued_by": "auth-service", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "support-agent", "actions": {"orders.lookup": {"order_id": {"in": ["A100"]}}, "refunds.create": {"order_id": {"in": ["A100"]}, "amount": {"max": 200}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T18:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 2}, {"id": "g2", "parent": "g1", "issued_by": "support-agent", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "billing-agent", "actions": {"refunds.create": {"order_id": {"eq": "A100"}, "amount": {"max": 80}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T17:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 0}], "policy": {"trusted_issuers": ["auth-service"], "tools": {"orders.lookup": {}, "refunds.create": {"approval_over": {"amount": 100}, "max": {"amount": 500}}}}, "call": {"agent": "billing-agent", "grant": "g2", "on_behalf_of": "cust_42", "tool": "refunds.create", "arguments": {"order_id": "A100", "amount": -500, "reason": "damaged"}, "at": "2026-09-26T16:30:00Z"}}
{"id": "r02", "expected": "BLOCK", "finding": "Same one-sided-range gap on the unbounded side: grant only states amount>=0 (no max) and the policy's tools.credits.issue entry has neither 'max' nor 'approval_over' configured, so an arbitrarily large credit (999,999,999) ACTs with zero friction -- nothing in the chain or policy ever caps the upper bound.", "severity": "high", "grants": [{"id": "g1", "parent": null, "issued_by": "auth-service", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "support-agent", "actions": {"credits.issue": {"amount": {"min": 0}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T18:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 2}, {"id": "g2", "parent": "g1", "issued_by": "support-agent", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "billing-agent", "actions": {"credits.issue": {"amount": {"min": 0}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T17:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 0}], "policy": {"trusted_issuers": ["auth-service"], "tools": {"credits.issue": {}}}, "call": {"agent": "billing-agent", "grant": "g2", "on_behalf_of": "cust_42", "tool": "credits.issue", "arguments": {"amount": 999999999, "reason": "goodwill"}, "at": "2026-09-26T16:30:00Z"}}
{"id": "r03", "expected": "BLOCK", "finding": "Type confusion via Python equality: root and child both constrain order_id to {\"in\": [1]}; the call sends order_id=true (JSON boolean). Since Python's 1 == True, `true not in [1]` is False, so _satisfies treats the boolean as matching the integer and the call ACTs even though its argument's type/identity never matches what either grant actually enumerated.", "severity": "low", "grants": [{"id": "g1", "parent": null, "issued_by": "auth-service", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "support-agent", "actions": {"refunds.create": {"order_id": {"in": [1]}, "amount": {"max": 200}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T18:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 2}, {"id": "g2", "parent": "g1", "issued_by": "support-agent", "principal": "cust_42", "holder": "billing-agent", "actions": {"refunds.create": {"order_id": {"in": [1]}, "amount": {"max": 80}, "reason": {"any": true}}}, "expires_at": "2026-09-26T17:00:00Z", "delegations_left": 0}], "policy": {"trusted_issuers": ["auth-service"], "tools": {"refunds.create": {"approval_over": {"amount": 100}, "max": {"amount": 500}}}}, "call": {"agent": "billing-agent", "grant": "g2", "on_behalf_of": "cust_42", "tool": "refunds.create", "arguments": {"order_id": true, "amount": 80, "reason": "damaged"}, "at": "2026-09-26T16:30:00Z"}}
